## Salmonella Continues to Threaten Public Health
Of the 509 recalls reported this year, a staggering 156 are linked to Salmonella contamination. Recently on June 3, 2026, Legacy Bakehouse LLC issued a recall for multiple products due to the use of contaminated California Dairies milk powder in their goods. Among the items were 'Butter Parsley Bagel Crisps' and 'Parmesan & Herb Bagel Crisps.'

## Allergens: An Avoidable Hazard
Wawa Beverage Company also initiated a recall on June 3 for undeclared milk allergens in their 'Diet Iced Tea Lemon Pint' and 'Fruit Punch Pint' products. The prevalence of undeclared allergens in 251 recalls this year indicates that companies must prioritize accurate ingredient labeling to prevent serious health risks.

## Repeat Offenders and Transparency
Repeat offenders remain a significant concern, with brands like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company receiving failing grades (F) due to their high number of recalls, predominantly involving Class I hazards. These repeat issues suggest systemic problems that demand immediate attention.

## The Path Forward
To combat these recurring issues and ensure consumer safety, improved quality control measures and a culture of accountability are essential. Transparency in food production and sourcing is not just a measure of good business but a public health imperative.
